12
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
The Island is a 2005 American science fiction action film directed and co-produced by Michael Bay and
written by Caspian Tredwell-Owen, Alex Kurtzman and Roberto Orci, from a story by Tredwell-Owen.

13
01:20:21,818 --> 01:20:27,818
It stars Ewan McGregor, Scarlett Johansson, Djimon Hounsou, Sean
Bean, Michael Clarke Duncan, and Steve Buscemi.

14
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:38,727
The film is about two human clones, Lincoln Six Echo (McGregor) and Jordan Two Delta
(Johansson), who live in a utopian compound isolated from the outside world.

15
01:32:43,636 --> 01:32:49,636
After Lincoln learns that the compound inhabitants are clones used for organ harvesting as well as surrogacy
for wealthy people, the two escape with the goal of exposing the illegal cloning movement.

16
01:38:54,545 --> 01:39:00,545
The Island has been described as a pastiche of "escape-from-dystopia" science fiction films of the 1960s
and 1970s, such as Fahrenheit 451, THX 1138, Parts: The Clonus Horror, and Logan's Run.

17
01:45:05,454 --> 01:45:11,454
The Island cost $126 million to produce.

18
01:51:16,363 --> 01:51:22,363
It opened on July 22, 2005, by DreamWorks Pictures in North
America and internationally by Warner Bros.

19
01:57:27,272 --> 01:57:33,272
Pictures, to mixed reviews, earning $36 million at the United States box office
and $127 million overseas for a $162 million worldwide total.

20
02:03:38,181 --> 02:03:44,181
The film explores themes of genetics, love of one's
life, escape, freedom, dystopia.

21
02:09:49,090 --> 02:09:55,090
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
